{
  "id": 1003,
  "name": "Post a Slack alert when any workflow fails",
  "description": "## What it does\n\nListens for failed executions with the **Error Trigger** and posts the workflow name, execution id and error message to Slack.\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Add a **Slack** credential.\n2. Replace `#alerts` with the channel you want to use.\n3. Activate this workflow — an Error Trigger workflow only fires once it is active.\n4. In every workflow you want to monitor, open **Settings → Error workflow** and select this workflow (or configure an instance-wide default). Activation alone does not subscribe other workflows.\n\n## Notes\n\nThe Error Trigger runs once per failed execution. If several workflows fail at the same time you get one message per failure; add a Merge node if you would rather batch them.",
